[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2613808446","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6872#issuecomment-2613808446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6872","id":2613808446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs6by40-","user":{"login":"saksham-sak","id":193908379,"node_id":"U_kgDOC47Omw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/193908379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak","html_url":"https://github.com/saksham-sak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saksham-sak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T06:31:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T12:14:29Z","body":" Ensure that each thread creates and uses its own ssl_context rather than sharing a global one. This isolates SSL configurations and avoids concurrency issues.\n Use requests' Session object and configure a unique SSL context per session.\nimport requests\nfrom urllib3.util.ssl_ import create_urllib3_context\n\ndef do_request():\n    session = requests.Session()\n    session.mount(\"https://\", requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter(\n        pool_connections=1, pool_maxsize=1, ssl_context=create_urllib3_context()\n    ))\n\n    cert = ('./client.crt', './client.key')\n    response = session.get(\"https://httpbin.org/anything\", cert=cert)\n    print(response.status_code)\n Avoids race conditions by isolating SSL contexts.\nSlightly increases memory usage due to creating multiple SSL contexts.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2613808446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"spam"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2616795592","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6872#issuecomment-2616795592","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6872","id":2616795592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs6b-SHI","user":{"login":"alloni","id":9369807,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzNjk4MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9369807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni","html_url":"https://github.com/alloni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T20:13:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T20:13:59Z","body":"@saksham-sak - that's fine for a workaround - and I will be implementing that - but it would still be a good idea to add a mutex around the SSL context read/update to prevent this happening to anyone _else_.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2616795592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2617220774","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6872#issuecomment-2617220774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6872","id":2617220774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs6b_56m","user":{"login":"sigmavirus24","id":240830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDgzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24","html_url":"https://github.com/sigmavirus24","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmavirus24/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T23:58:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T23:58:54Z","body":"If you're finding that an SSLContext is not thread safe you should instead file that bug with CPython, with the most minimal reproduction case possible in order to get a real fix. I know for a fact it disables the GIL in _ssl.c and uses openssl's locking logic, so it's also possible this an OpenSSL issue although I imagine something like this would have already been found. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2617220774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2619594968","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/6872#issuecomment-2619594968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/6872","id":2619594968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABTKOs6cI9jY","user":{"login":"alloni","id":9369807,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzNjk4MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9369807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni","html_url":"https://github.com/alloni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alloni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T17:10:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T17:10:08Z","body":"@sigmavirus24 - Looks like this _is_ documented in CPython - as per https://docs.python.org/3/library/ssl.html#ssl.SSLContext:\n\n`Note - SSLContext is designed to be shared and used by multiple connections. Thus, it is thread-safe as long as it is not reconfigured after being used by a connection.`\n\nSo it's explicitly documented as not thread-safe under these circumstances.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/2619594968/reactions","total_count":0